WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.360
Alright, what have I done?

00:03.360 --> 00:05.400
So, there's a lot of things going on here.

00:05.400 --> 00:06.400
These are stickers.

00:06.400 --> 00:12.200
I'm here at the cafe called Missong, space here in Bangkok.

00:12.200 --> 00:17.000
So I just think that maybe I can use this opportunity where I'm just playing around with the stickers,

00:17.000 --> 00:21.640
which is one of the things I like the most when it comes to leisure stuff, to teach you

00:21.640 --> 00:25.600
a little bit about how AI actually works on categorizing data.

00:25.600 --> 00:30.600
Like we've been talking a lot about how we should be using AI in terms of making our life easier.

00:30.600 --> 00:36.800
So if you have a bucket of two thousands, no, two hundred, sticker like this, how do you categorize it?

00:36.800 --> 00:39.600
So AI would do three things for you.

00:39.600 --> 00:43.000
So first thing first, you have to tell AI how to categorize it.

00:43.000 --> 00:49.600
So for instance, on the whole issue of different stickers, AI might probably pick up some of the things that,

00:49.600 --> 00:54.800
like this for instance, pick this up, then you have to tell AI that, okay, this is category A.

00:55.000 --> 00:56.000
Winnie the Pooh.

00:56.000 --> 01:01.200
So every time I find anything that looks similar, we're going to pull them together.

01:01.200 --> 01:04.000
So you have a big pile of, Winnie the Pooh here.

01:04.000 --> 01:07.000
Or this is Boo Boo and Lulu, really cute.

01:07.000 --> 01:10.500
So you're going to have to tell AI first that this is Boo Boo and Lulu category B.

01:10.500 --> 01:16.100
So every time I find anything that looks like this, I will just put them all in the same pile like this together.

01:16.100 --> 01:19.200
So you see how fast that things could actually go.

01:19.200 --> 01:27.000
But if AI doesn't have the understanding for a fact that this could actually look like Boo Boo, right?

01:27.000 --> 01:29.700
So if that's the case, this is Lulu or Boo Boo anyway.

01:29.700 --> 01:33.800
The point is that AI will ask you and you tell that this is not this,

01:33.800 --> 01:36.000
which means that they will go into category C.

01:36.000 --> 01:40.000
And then once you keep building it up, you're using the first of all,

01:40.000 --> 01:44.200
the supervised learning where you tell AI that this is in the category A.

01:44.200 --> 01:45.200
Winnie the Pooh.

01:45.200 --> 01:48.400
This is in the category B, Boo Boo and Lulu.

01:48.400 --> 01:52.600
This is in category C, maybe all the letters and stuff.

01:52.600 --> 01:57.400
Then if the AI doesn't understand that he will ask you when we put this category in,

01:57.400 --> 01:59.900
then you can tell AI that this goes into category E.

01:59.900 --> 02:03.100
And right now we have category A all the way to category Z.

02:03.100 --> 02:06.200
And that's actually category A1 and B1, Z1, and this pool.

02:06.200 --> 02:11.500
But as you see, what AI is doing here is to learn from you, right?

02:11.500 --> 02:17.600
But because AI doesn't see Boo Boo and Lulu like you, AI see grains and patterns of colors.

02:17.600 --> 02:23.100
So you have to tell it exactly that this is a grain and color that has a tendency to be what you want.

02:23.100 --> 02:27.000
And once it categorizes for you, you can actually check and see whether this is right.

02:27.000 --> 02:27.900
I think this is right.

02:27.900 --> 02:33.400
We actually continue to reinforce the learning that this is the right category that you should put things into.

02:33.400 --> 02:38.600
And within the next few stages or sessions of learning, AI will do even faster.

02:38.600 --> 02:42.900
And I can tell by my own experiences here that even I do it with my own eyes,

02:42.900 --> 02:44.900
I get faster and faster every time, right?

02:44.900 --> 02:48.200
AI is able to learn faster and faster every time as well.

02:48.200 --> 02:51.600
So once you are able to do that, you can actually categorize this very easily

02:51.600 --> 02:57.600
and use AI to make your life better because these are repetitive tasks that machine learning can do really well.

02:57.600 --> 03:00.900
So again, there will be a lot of things that I can share with you,

03:00.900 --> 03:06.500
but I think this would be a good lesson to learn in terms of why is it that we should be using AI

03:06.500 --> 03:13.000
to do things that it can do more effectively than our eyes and brains and labor and of course time.

03:13.000 --> 03:14.500
Until then, thank you.

